    # scipy.stats.distributions.burr12_gen
    {
        "name":        'burr12_gen',
        "color":       '#7A4A8A',
        "category":    'scipy/stats/distributions',
        "description": 'A Burr (Type XII) continuous random variable.\n\n%(before_notes)s\n\nSee Also\n--------\nfisk : a special case of either `burr` or `burr12` with ``d=1``\nburr : Burr Type III distribution\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe probability density function for `burr12` is:\n\n.. math::\n\n    f(x; c, d) = c d \\frac{x^{c-1}}\n                          {(1 + x^c)^{d + 1}}\n\nfor :math:`x >= 0` and :math:`c, d > 0`.\n\n`burr12` takes ``c`` and ``d`` as shape parameters for :math:`c`\nand :math:`d`.\n\nThis is the PDF corresponding to the twelfth CDF given in Burr\'s list;\nspecifically, it is equation (20) in Burr\'s paper [1]_.\n\n%(after_notes)s\n\nThe Burr type 12 distribution is also sometimes referred to as\nthe Singh-Maddala distribution from NIST [2]_.\n\nReferences\n----------\n.. [1] Burr, I. W. "Cumulative frequency functions", Annals of\n   Mathematical Statistics, 13(2), pp 215-232 (1942).\n\n.. [2] https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/software/dataplot/refman2/auxillar/b12pdf.htm\n\n.. [3] "Burr distribution",\n   https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burr_distribution\n\n%(example)s',
        "inputs": [
            ('momtype', 'any', 'Default: 1', '1'),
            ('a', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('b', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('xtol', 'any', 'Default: 1e-14', '1e-14'),
            ('badvalue', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('name', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('longname', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('shapes', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('seed', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
        ],
        "outputs": [
            ('burr12_gen', 'object', 'Result of scipy.stats.distributions.burr12_gen'),
        ],
    },

    # scipy.stats.distributions.burr_gen
    {
        "name":        'burr_gen',
        "color":       '#7A4A8A',
        "category":    'scipy/stats/distributions',
        "description": 'A Burr (Type III) continuous random variable.\n\n%(before_notes)s\n\nSee Also\n--------\nfisk : a special case of either `burr` or `burr12` with ``d=1``\nburr12 : Burr Type XII distribution\nmielke : Mielke Beta-Kappa / Dagum distribution\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe probability density function for `burr` is:\n\n.. math::\n\n    f(x; c, d) = c d \\frac{x^{-c - 1}}\n                          {{(1 + x^{-c})}^{d + 1}}\n\nfor :math:`x >= 0` and :math:`c, d > 0`.\n\n`burr` takes ``c`` and ``d`` as shape parameters for :math:`c` and\n:math:`d`.\n\nThis is the PDF corresponding to the third CDF given in Burr\'s list;\nspecifically, it is equation (11) in Burr\'s paper [1]_. The distribution\nis also commonly referred to as the Dagum distribution [2]_. If the\nparameter :math:`c < 1` then the mean of the distribution does not\nexist and if :math:`c < 2` the variance does not exist [2]_.\nThe PDF is finite at the left endpoint :math:`x = 0` if :math:`c * d >= 1`.\n\n%(after_notes)s\n\nReferences\n----------\n.. [1] Burr, I. W. "Cumulative frequency functions", Annals of\n   Mathematical Statistics, 13(2), pp 215-232 (1942).\n.. [2] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagum_distribution\n.. [3] Kleiber, Christian. "A guide to the Dagum distributions."\n   Modeling Income Distributions and Lorenz Curves  pp 97-117 (2008).\n\n%(example)s',
        "inputs": [
            ('momtype', 'any', 'Default: 1', '1'),
            ('a', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('b', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('xtol', 'any', 'Default: 1e-14', '1e-14'),
            ('badvalue', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('name', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('longname', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('shapes', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('seed', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
        ],
        "outputs": [
            ('burr_gen', 'object', 'Result of scipy.stats.distributions.burr_gen'),
        ],
    },

