    # scipy.stats.distributions.geom_gen
    {
        "name":        'geom_gen',
        "color":       '#7A4A8A',
        "category":    'scipy/stats/distributions',
        "description": 'A geometric discrete random variable.\n\n%(before_notes)s\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe probability mass function for `geom` is:\n\n.. math::\n\n    f(k) = (1-p)^{k-1} p\n\nfor :math:`k \\ge 1`, :math:`0 < p \\leq 1`\n\n`geom` takes :math:`p` as shape parameter,\nwhere :math:`p` is the probability of a single success\nand :math:`1-p` is the probability of a single failure.\n\nNote that when drawing random samples, the probability of observations that exceed\n``np.iinfo(np.int64).max`` increases rapidly as $p$ decreases below $10^{-17}$. For\n$p < 10^{-20}$, almost all observations would exceed the maximum ``int64``; however,\nthe output dtype is always ``int64``, so these values are clipped to the maximum.\n\n%(after_notes)s\n\nSee Also\n--------\nplanck\n\n%(example)s',
        "inputs": [
            ('a', 'any', 'Default: 0', '0'),
            ('b', 'any', 'Default: inf', 'inf'),
            ('name', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('badvalue', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('moment_tol', 'any', 'Default: 1e-08', '1e-08'),
            ('values', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('inc', 'any', 'Default: 1', '1'),
            ('longname', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('shapes', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
            ('seed', 'any', 'Default: None', 'None'),
        ],
        "outputs": [
            ('geom_gen', 'object', 'Result of scipy.stats.distributions.geom_gen'),
        ],
    },

